From 1fee8aaa172273473c42092e256b73fdf14054cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:06:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] intel_extreme: reject allocation sizes that exceed the ioctl
 ABI

The accelerant accepts size_t but the private graphics allocation request carries a uint32 size. Reject zero and oversized requests before narrowing so a large buffer cannot silently become a smaller allocation. Preserve the caller output address on rejected requests.

Tested 111 actual-function size-boundary cases with address and undefined-behavior sanitizers and no exceptions or RTTI. The prior source fails 104 truncation/boundary assertions. Native compilation remains pending.

Assisted-by: Codex
Signed-off-by: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/add-ons/accelerants/intel_extreme/memory.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/accelerants/intel_extreme/memory.cpp b/src/add-ons/accelerants/intel_extreme/memory.cpp
index 731b972b..c5adcf03 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/accelerants/intel_extreme/memory.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/accelerants/intel_extreme/memory.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "intel_extreme.h"
 
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
 
@@ -44,6 +45,11 @@ intel_free_memory(addr_t base)
 status_t
 intel_allocate_memory(size_t size, uint32 flags, addr_t &base)
 {
+	// The private ioctl carries a 32-bit size even on x86_64. Reject
+	// requests that would wrap into a smaller allocation before narrowing.
+	if (size == 0 || size > UINT32_MAX)
+		return B_BAD_VALUE;
+
 	intel_allocate_graphics_memory allocMemory;
 	allocMemory.magic = INTEL_PRIVATE_DATA_MAGIC;
 	allocMemory.size = size;
